  "note": "The getomni schema keeps the three header identifiers and one shipment out of the three printed, and even for that shipment it omits the reference number, service type and base charge. Extended with the remaining header values (title, carrier, page) and a 'shipments' array covering all three printed rows with every column of the table, including each additional-charge line's amount, VAT/Code and gross value. The dataset's 'issueDate', 'clientNumber', 'documentNumber' and 'mostRecentShipment' are preserved unchanged; 'shipments[2]' is that shipment recorded in full, and it is the row that carries the reference number 'WH4EHYLISO' the dataset left out. All added values corroborated against the 14 saved engine outputs. Judgement calls: (1) reference number is blank on the first two rows and recorded as null; (2) the weight 40 is printed without a decimal and kept that way; (3) 'FORT DELLAFURT, 76630-3695' sits at 3 of 14 as a whole string only because most engines wrap that cell — the zip code half of it is the dataset's own recipient zipCode, so the reading is not in doubt; (4) the table has a long tail of blank ruled rows below the third shipment, which carry no data and are not represented.",
  "extended_annotator": "claude-opus-5",
